From: HaeImAlan <me@haeimalan.com>
Subject: remoteproc: qcom_q6v5_mpd: make MSA/internal-wifi SCM calls optional

The multi-PD WCSS driver issues qcom_scm_msa_lock() /
qcom_scm_msa_unlock() around every user-PD start/stop, plus
qcom_scm_internal_wifi_powerup() / qcom_scm_internal_wifi_shutdown()
for the internal radio's PD (pd_asid == 1).

These are vendor-specific SCM command IDs. Qualcomm's own QSDK
multi-PD driver for IPQ5018 (qcom_q6v5_mpd.c in the 5.4-qsdk tree)
never issues them -- it uses only qcom_scm_pas_auth_and_reset() and
qcom_scm_pas_shutdown() -- and drives both the internal IPQ5018 radio
and an external QCN6122 successfully on IPQ5018-era TrustZone.

On boards running an older stock IPQ5018 TrustZone (e.g. the Xiaomi
AX3000E, BOOT.BF.3.3.1.1-00064) these command IDs are not implemented.
Invoking them faults on the secure side, which kills the CPU with no
kernel-visible error: an immediate cold reset back to PBL, with no oops
and no panic. This made enabling QCN6122 (which switches q6v5_wcss from
"qcom,ipq5018-wcss-sec-pil" to "qcom,ipq5018-q6-mpd") appear to be a
QCN6122 problem, when the trigger is actually the compatible swap alone.

Patch 0818 ("skip MSA lock for internal radio") already skips the MSA
lock/unlock on IPQ5018, but only for pd_asid 1. It still issues the
MSA lock for the QCN6122 PDs and still calls the internal-wifi
powerup/shutdown for pd_asid 1, and any one of those cold-resets the
AX3000E. 0818's own trigger corroborates the underlying problem: the
Wallys DR5018S TrustZone rejects the MSA lock for PASID 0x112 with
-EINVAL. IPQ5018 TrustZone builds differ in which of these SCM IDs
they implement, and on the AX3000E the failure is a reset rather than
an error code, so nothing short of skipping all of them is safe.

Add a no_msa_scm flag on top of 0818 that skips the MSA lock/unlock
for every PD and the internal-wifi calls, and set it for IPQ5018 to
match QSDK's proven sequence. Other SoCs keep the existing behaviour.
wcss_pd_start() now returns 0 explicitly: with every SCM call skipped,
a PD without a spawn bit would otherwise return an uninitialised ret.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: HaeImAlan <me@haeimalan.com>

--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_mpd.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_mpd.c
@@ -100,6 +100,7 @@ struct wcss_data {
 	u32 pasid;
 	bool share_upd_info_to_q6;
 	bool skip_msa_lock_internal_radio;
+	bool no_msa_scm;
 	u8 bootargs_version;
 };
 
@@ -165,8 +166,9 @@ static int wcss_pd_start(struct rproc *rproc)
 	struct rproc *rpd_rproc = dev_get_drvdata(upd->dev->parent);
 	struct q6_wcss *wcss = rpd_rproc->priv;
 	u32 pasid = (upd->pd_asid << 8) | UPD_SWID;
-	bool skip_msa_lock = wcss->desc->skip_msa_lock_internal_radio &&
-			     upd->pd_asid == 1;
+	bool skip_msa_lock = wcss->desc->no_msa_scm ||
+			     (wcss->desc->skip_msa_lock_internal_radio &&
+			      upd->pd_asid == 1);
 	int ret;
 
 	if (!skip_msa_lock) {
@@ -183,7 +185,7 @@ static int wcss_pd_start(struct rproc *rproc)
 			return ret;
 	}
 
-	if (upd->pd_asid == 1) {
+	if (upd->pd_asid == 1 && !wcss->desc->no_msa_scm) {
 		ret = qcom_scm_internal_wifi_powerup(wcss->desc->pasid);
 		if (ret) {
 			dev_err(upd->dev, "failed to power up internal radio\n");
@@ -191,7 +193,7 @@ static int wcss_pd_start(struct rproc *rproc)
 		}
 	}
 
-	return ret;
+	return 0;
 }
 
 static int q6_wcss_stop(struct rproc *rproc)
@@ -247,8 +249,9 @@ static int wcss_pd_stop(struct rproc *rproc)
 	struct rproc *rpd_rproc = dev_get_drvdata(upd->dev->parent);
 	struct q6_wcss *wcss = rpd_rproc->priv;
 	u32 pasid = (upd->pd_asid << 8) | UPD_SWID;
-	bool skip_msa_lock = wcss->desc->skip_msa_lock_internal_radio &&
-			     upd->pd_asid == 1;
+	bool skip_msa_lock = wcss->desc->no_msa_scm ||
+			     (wcss->desc->skip_msa_lock_internal_radio &&
+			      upd->pd_asid == 1);
 	int ret;
 
 	if (rproc->state != RPROC_CRASHED && upd->q6.stop_bit) {
@@ -259,7 +262,7 @@ static int wcss_pd_stop(struct rproc *rproc)
 		}
 	}
 
-	if (upd->pd_asid == 1) {
+	if (upd->pd_asid == 1 && !wcss->desc->no_msa_scm) {
 		ret = qcom_scm_internal_wifi_shutdown(wcss->desc->pasid);
 		if (ret) {
 			dev_err(upd->dev, "failed to power down internal radio\n");
@@ -855,6 +858,7 @@ static const struct wcss_data q6_ipq5018_res_init = {
 	.pasid = MPD_WCNSS_PAS_ID,
 	.share_upd_info_to_q6 = true,
 	.skip_msa_lock_internal_radio = true,
+	.no_msa_scm = true,
 	.bootargs_version = VERSION1,
 	// .mdt_load_sec = qcom_mdt_load_pd_seg,
 };
